xmodel/pi1s4-84-row-kill-opus5-20260901.log:8:**Theorem A (§1.2, unconditional).** For monic `(P,Q)` of degrees `(8,4)`, the identity `ord_s(w − v²) = 16 − deg(P−Q²)` makes the row label `δ₂ = 6` *equivalent* to `deg(P−Q²) = 6`. So the shear `Φ(x,y) = (x−y², y)` carries **every** member of the (8,4) row onto a (6,4) row member (degrees (6,4), `A₁₄` at infinity, same three nodes), and back. This upgrades the coordinator's provisional witness-level equivalence to a row-level theorem.
xmodel/pi1s4-84-row-kill-opus5-20260901.log:12:**On the binding non-transfer note.** It is correct — for everything it was actually about. The projective closure, the germ, `M∞`, the `B₆`/`B₈` tuples, `γ∞` (`6g` vs `8g`), the fold, and the branch degree all fail to transport, and §4 tabulates each. What transports is the pair `(A², D)` up to `Aut(A²)`, hence the group with its meridian class. TRIPLE-COVER-CLOSE §6 had already stated that principle; the two things blocking its use — a monogenicity-conditional (6,4) theorem, and witness-only equivalence — are both now gone.
xmodel/pi1s4-84-row-kill-opus5-20260901.log:16:- **§2, Lemma NO-FOLD (unconditional):** `P` is never a perfect square on the row, so `x = s(t)²` and `x = u(t)⁴` are both excluded. There are 7 simple vertical tangencies with no identity-forced simultaneity; the (6,4) collision at `x = 0` is an artefact of `p = r²`. INF-TRIVIAL has no analogue, and I did not manufacture one — `ψ(γ∞) = 1` is typed `OPEN` (and is vacuous on this row).
