xmodel/sol-approaches.log:1938:- **Helali:** Zenodo **10.5281/zenodo.21479814** v1.0.1, pub. 2026-07-21 — "Exact Computer-Assisted Exclusion of the (72,108) Frontier in the Two-Dimensional Jacobian Problem" + GitHub `bilLkarkariy/jc2-72-108-exact-certificates` (1 star, 5 commits). Claim structure: transcribes BOTH residual systems of GGHV Prop 4.3; Case 2 killed by a unit-ideal identity 1 = ΣT_iR_i; Case 1 splits into s=±c branches, an identity forces h=0, unit-ideal certificates kill the h=0 specialization; an involution transports the hard certificate between sign branches. Hard certificate 89,105,967 bytes; multiplier ansatz a 2010×1925 rational linear system, fixed 1925×1925 minor with det 10 mod 71; independent gmpy2 replay of 13,410 number-field products, ~70 s on a laptop, marker `JC2_72_108_EXACT_REPLAY_PASS`. **Explicitly conditional** on correctness + faithful transcription of GGHV's reduction; explicitly "not a proof of JC(2)". AI disclosure: OpenAI Codex. No arXiv (no endorsement), no expert audit visible. [COMPETES-WITH-US — inspectable, plausible, unaudited]
xmodel/sol-approaches.log:1939:- **Suzuki (Eiki Suzuki, ORCID 0009-0002-0556-4967):** Zenodo **10.5281/zenodo.21483636** v1.1.4, pub. 2026-07-22 — "Exclusion of the (8,28) Newton-Polygon Case in the Plane Jacobian Conjecture" (EN+JA PDFs + 5.1 MB verification ZIP with negative controls). **This is exactly our A0=(8,28) family.** Method is structural, not brute-force: **5 dessin-d'enfants classes for the top-edge equation**, Bézout identity via exact elimination over a degree-5 number field, weighted Macaulay 261×261 minor with det ≡ 21 mod 23. Claims both alternatives excluded ⇒ bound 108 → 125. [COMPETES-WITH-US and USABLE-BY-US — small certificates, and the 5-class top-edge classification is directly relevant to our leading-tower combinatorics]
