xmodel/ggv-qgate-opus-new-claims-hostile-review-grok46-20260827.md:96:**Injectivity.** `T_Q(Q)=0` rearranges to `Q'/Q=(3/2)A'/A+(1/4)B'/B`, i.e. `Q^4 \sim A^6 B`. On squarefree coprime `(A,B)` the valuations 6 (at `A`-roots) and 1 (at `B`-roots) are not divisible by 4, so the kernel is empty over any characteristic-zero field. Exact criterion, slightly sharper than "empty": `A^6 B` is not a fourth power in `K(X)`. At these degrees that is equivalent to the squarefree-coprime package. Nullspace of the `12\times 16` matrix is trivial on five fixtures, and remains trivial for `deg Q<=20`.
