xmodel/td6-boundary-qb-pencil-review-grok-20260824.md:128:Independent field presentation. `F=24S^6-252S^5+1170S^4-3045S^3+4680S^2-4032S+1411` satisfies `F=0` in `K` by construction. `gcd(F,F')=1` over `Q`, so `F` is squarefree. Rabin’s criterion modulo 31 (prime divisors of six are 2 and 3) gives `gcd(F, x^{31^2}-x)=1`, `gcd(F, x^{31^3}-x)=1`, and `x^{31^6}≡x`, so `F` is irreducible over `F_{31}` and therefore over `Q`. Thus `K=Q[S]/(F)` is a degree-6 field.
