xmodel/as109-one-sided-prime4-composition-hostile-review-grok-20260827.md:238:Both include `H=0`. Independently checked on `m=1..240` and `H=0..120` with zero failures. History-stop also closes `d=3` when `3` does not divide `H` (sheared total gcd prime), which is the same cell as `d=3 => 3|H`. For `d=6`, history-stop only forces `gcd(H,6) not in {1,2}`; `6|H` is strictly stronger and comes from Theorem 2.7 plus the UFD, not from the `gcd<=2` shear.
