xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3753:RECON.md:52:- **Suzuki (Eiki Suzuki, ORCID 0009-0002-0556-4967):** Zenodo **10.5281/zenodo.21483636** v1.1.4, pub. 2026-07-22 — "Exclusion of the (8,28) Newton-Polygon Case in the Plane Jacobian Conjecture" (EN+JA PDFs + 5.1 MB verification ZIP with negative controls). **This is exactly our A0=(8,28) family.** Method is structural, not brute-force: **5 dessin-d'enfants classes for the top-edge equation**, Bézout identity via exact elimination over a degree-5 number field, weighted Macaulay 261×261 minor with det ≡ 21 mod 23. Claims both alternatives excluded ⇒ bound 108 → 125. [COMPETES-WITH-US and USABLE-BY-US — small certificates, and the 5-class top-edge classification is directly relevant to our leading-tower combinatorics]
xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3759:RECON.md:89:- **Speyer / Secret Blogging Seminar (2026-07-20)** (sbseminar.wordpress.com/2026/07/20/the-new-counterexample-to-the-jacobian-conjecture/): notes the seed map's homogeneity under deg(x,y,z)=(−1,1,2); discriminants factor as squares; sheets "escape to infinity together" over Δ=0. Comment thread is the sharpest public structure discussion: **Will Sawin** (07-20) gives the P^1×Sym^2(P^1)→Sym^3(P^1) formulation with X ≅ A^3 as iterated A^1-bundle; **"Skooi"** (07-21) proves the direct generalization π: P^1×P^(d−1)→P^d **fails for d ≥ 4 by a Picard/class-group obstruction (discriminant class Z/(d−2)) — "only d=3 threads the needle"**; Lior Silberman raises char-2 (answered by 2607.20968). [USABLE-BY-US — the obstruction calculus for why the mechanism needs d=3 is the best current hint at what a dim-2 mechanism must evade]
