xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:40:**F6. Braun–Gwoździewicz–Fernandes–Oréfice-Okamoto, *A sharp degree bound in the real Jacobian conjecture*, arXiv:2605.12302v2, 2026-05-24.** SHA-256 `f1aa8f3416bd2bf17afe271100b3b08391952597f0736a2921057a518e9d3d5f`. Real plane maps with nowhere-zero Jacobian: injective if \(\deg p\le 6\); a noninjective example at \(\deg p=7\). Settles the real degree bound. **IRRELEVANT** to complex JC2 (Pinchuk-type real maps already have nonconstant Jacobian over \(\mathbb{C}\)).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:58:**F11. Corral–Gómez-Martínez–Senovilla-Sanz, *Cuspidal dicritical foliations and analytical invariants of cusps*, arXiv:2605.30634v1, 2026-05-28.** SHA-256 `d3bc4da7093756084cada50f9eb0a90344d9108aae488454fcb42b999e176cd1`. Local germs of foliations on \((\mathbb{C}^2,0)\): a foliation is *cuspidal dicritical* if after the minimal resolution of a cusp it is totally \(E\)-dicritical along the cuspidal divisor. The invariant curves through free points of \(E\) are equisingular cusps, not in general analytically equivalent. Main theorems: \(\ell\)-transversality with a minimal standard basis of 1-forms freezes the first \(\ell+2\) generators of the semimodule \(\Lambda_C\) of differential values; a bound on the divisorial value \(\nu_E(\omega_{\mathcal{F}})\) in terms of the conductor of \(\Lambda_C\) forces \(\Lambda\)-constancy of the whole family. Explicit conductor formula \(c(\Lambda_C)=\tilde u_{s+1}-n-m+1\). **STRUCTURE** for the local analytic classification of one-Puiseux-pair branches and for the vocabulary “dicritical along a cusp.” **IRRELEVANT** as a close of Domrina–Orevkov or of a global polynomial Keller map: these are local foliations, not polynomial self-maps of \(\mathbb{A}^2\), and the Jacobian of a Keller map is a *constant*, not a foliation 1-form.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:80:**F18. Liu–Zhang, *On the discriminant locus of a generic projection*, arXiv:2603.21518v2, 2026-04-19.** SHA-256 `5aeeed618aae253e512090ad3a1c1dae85c649c8732924c5ca8d33195cac3324`. Discriminant of a generic projection of a smooth \(X\subset\mathbb{P}^N\) is projectively dual to a general linear section of the dual variety; over \(\mathbb{C}\), \(\pi_1\) of the complement of the branch divisor of a generic projection of a *normal hypersurface* surjects onto a braid group via braid monodromy. **STRUCTURE** for braid monodromy of generic projections, wrong geometry for residual one-place affine curves.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:122:Target: Heegaard–Floer / BLZ bounds for plane curves; equality cases. Bearing on the \((9,6,4)\) sharpness witness (HF-ATTAIN, `PASS_NECESSARY_ONLY`) and the six-nodal realized curve kill (representation-level, not Floer).
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:124:**F26. Kubasch–Schefler, *Lattice cohomology and the embedded topological type of plane curve singularities*, arXiv:2504.13366v1, 2025-04-17.** SHA-256 `3f2bd1e7c53079653577bfda62bc03751cf209d303e78bd3b77cd5a9acdc0ac4`. Analytic lattice cohomology of reduced curve singularities is an algebro-geometric analogue of Heegaard Floer Link homology in the plane case (and extends to higher codimension). For *irreducible* plane curve singularities, lattice cohomology is a **complete embedded topological invariant**. Comparison with the integral Seifert form for multiple branches. **STRUCTURE** for the HF/BLZ toolkit: a complete combinatorial stand-in for HFL of irreducible plane branches. **Does not** list additional saturating semigroups of BLZ Theorem 6.4, does not treat mixed nodal/\(A_3\) configurations, and does not mention \((9,6,4)\). **IRRELEVANT as news** to the campaign’s \((9,6,4)\) sharpness witness; **no threat** to the representation-level kill of the realized six-nodal curve (that kill is ZvK/S_4, not Floer).
