xmodel/as109-support-review-grok-20260824.md:173:Over `Z` already, `A_0=y^m` (`m>=1`) has vanishing `x`-derivative and `B_0=x^{108} y` has `y`-derivative `x^{108}`, so `E1` holds over `F_{109}` and over `Z`. Both polynomials vanish on `y=0`, hence at `(0,0)` and `(1,0)`, so the frozen collision differences are zero. The literal slots are exactly `(P,(0,m))` and `(Q,(108,1))`.
